<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 2.4 · Lunar, Cooking & Recipe for Disaster" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="2-4" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 2.4</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Lunar, Cooking & Recipe for Disaster</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Open Neitiznot and Lunar Isle, build a useful food stock while training Cooking, and free the five remaining Recipe for Disaster council members.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Complete The Fremennik Isles, Lunar Diplomacy, One Small Favour and Swan Song; reach unboosted 60 Mining and 70 Cooking; free the five council members Chapter 1 left frozen; defeat the Culinaromancer and buy Barrows gloves."
        stats={["60 Mining for Lunar Diplomacy (unboostable)", "65 Magic after the 1,590 High Alchs", "62 Cooking before Swan Song; 70 before Awowogei", "181 QP after the previous chapters; 202 on completion"]}
        unlocks={["Helm of Neitiznot, Lunar spellbook and Piscatoris", "Karambwan fishing/cooking and a permanent food loop", "Full Recipe for Disaster and Barrows gloves", "Two 10,000-XP Herblore lamps; final 20,000-XP lamp reserved for Herblore"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Before you begin:</strong> Chapter 1.3 completed the RFD introduction and freed the Goblin generals, Mountain Dwarf and Pirate Pete. Chapter 2.3 finished Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl and Horror from the Deep. Completing the previous chapters gives you <strong>181 Quest Points</strong>, enough for both Legends' Quest's 107-point start requirement and RFD's 175-point finale. Check your quest log for any unfinished steps if you followed a different order.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Fremennik and Lunar infrastructure</div><h2>Open Neitiznot and prepare for Lunar Diplomacy.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i24-isles" number="1" title="Complete The Fremennik Isles">
        <p><strong>Why now:</strong> The Fremennik Trials, 70 Woodcutting and 50+ Construction are already in place. The quest adds Neitiznot travel and the <strong>Helm of Neitiznot</strong>, a durable melee helm with a Prayer bonus. Take Mord Gunnars' boat from Rellekka to Jatizso, speak with King Gjuki Sorvott IV and work through the Jatizso/Neitiznot errands as one quest. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Fremennik_Isles" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki quest walkthrough</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Before travelling:</strong> bank <strong>one raw tuna, seven coal if your Mining is 2–54 or six mithril ore if it is 55+, and nine ropes</strong> (eight ropes if you already own the required shield), an axe, knife, <strong>hammer and bronze nail</strong>, needle and two thread, coins, food and teleports. Bring or make a <strong>Neitiznot shield</strong>: two arctic-pine logs, one rope and the bronze nail/hammer, not a shield bought from another player. Cut <strong>eight more arctic-pine logs and split them</strong> for bridge repair (56 Woodcutting required, already met), and make the yak-hide top and legs from local hides if not banked (46 Crafting, already met). Keep the shield for the troll section. You can take the normal route if you cannot use the mine shortcut.</p>
        <p>Rebank before the <strong>Ice Troll King</strong> (level 122): shield, food, prayer restore and solid melee gear are more important than rushing the final corridor. Kill <strong>ten frenzied ice trolls</strong> with the honour guards first; you can leave and restock before crossing to the king. His Magic/Ranged defence makes melee the practical default; the shield helps with troll ranged damage. Use <strong>Protect from Magic</strong> against the king and <strong>do not use Protect from Melee</strong>, which triggers his knockback attack. Read the linked fight guide if this is your first attempt. Claim the helm and two <strong>10,000-XP choices among Attack, Strength, Defence or Hitpoints</strong> when finished; put them into the combat skills you still need for the Warriors' Guild or Piety, then check your new levels. Keep the helm rather than treating it as a disposable quest prop.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Bring the king's fish and ore, then make the local equipment">
          <p>Buy the <strong>raw tuna from Flosi in east Jatizso</strong>, or fish it with a harpoon at the pier. The route's minimum Mining level is 50, which means <strong>seven coal</strong>; an account already at 55+ is asked for <strong>six mithril ore</strong> instead. Mine the missing ore in the underground mine northwest of Jatizso, or buy it from Ordan before travelling. Coal and mithril bars are not interchangeable with the requested ore.</p>
          <p>Buy missing ropes from Ned and a needle/thread from Dommik. Smith one bronze bar into bronze nails at an anvil if no nail remains. Cut <strong>ten arctic-pine logs in total</strong> when making everything: split eight at Neitiznot's central woodcutting stump for the two bridges, and keep two unsplit for the shield. Kill local yaks for <strong>three hides</strong>, pay Thakkrad beside Mawnis <strong>five coins per hide</strong> to cure them, and sew the two-hide top and one-hide legs. Check the shield and both armour pieces before the troll trip.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-mining-60" number="2" title="Train Mining from 50 to 60">
        <p><strong>Lunar Diplomacy requires unboosted 60 Mining.</strong> Check your level after 2.2 and train only as much as you still need. Stop at <strong>60</strong>; you will return for Making Friends with My Arm's 72-Mining requirement later.</p>
        <p><strong>Shooting Stars</strong> are the low-attention choice: locate a landed star via the in-game/world-tracking community, bring a pickaxe, mine a tier your level permits and move to the next star when it depletes. The 2,000 stardust Chapter 1 set aside already bought the celestial ring; any new dust is a bonus. <strong>Motherlode Mine</strong> is the resource-minded choice: mine pay-dirt, deposit it in the hopper, collect ore from the sack and bank it for later Smithing. It asks for more movement but turns this level gate into useful metal stock. If you independently unlocked Cam Torum, calcified deposits are another relaxed option; do not complete Perilous Moons just to enter them. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Mining_training" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki Mining methods</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i24-mining-methods" informational={true} skill="Mining" target="60, unboosted" why="Lunar's Mining gate is unboostable; 72 for Making Friends belongs in 2.6." recommended="Shooting Stars for long low-attention sessions, stopping when the skill tab reads 60." resource="Motherlode Mine pay-dirt for ore that later supports Smithing." relaxed="Calcified deposits only if Cam Torum is already unlocked independently." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-lunar" number="3" title="Check the requirements and complete Lunar Diplomacy">
        <p><strong>Required levels and quests:</strong> Lunar needs unboosted <strong>5 Herblore, 61 Crafting, 40 Defence, 49 Firemaking, 65 Magic, 60 Mining and 55 Woodcutting</strong>, plus The Fremennik Trials, Lost City, Rune Mysteries and Shilo Village. The Mining training above finishes the remaining skill requirement. The 1,590 High Alchs in 2.1 gave <strong>103,350 Magic XP</strong>, enough to reach 65 from level 63 (368,599 XP, compared with 449,428 XP for level 65). The Defence rewards in 2.2, including Daero's selected 35,000 XP, bring you past 40 Defence. Check both in the skill tab before departure.</p>
        <p><strong>Bring:</strong> bring a pickaxe, axe, hammer, tinderbox, spade, needle and two thread, pestle and mortar, a working bullseye lantern (the banked sapphire lantern from Tears of Guthix works), guam and marrentill, roughly 1,000 coins, a <strong>dramen staff</strong>, food and combat supplies. Bring access to the <strong>air, fire, water and earth altars</strong> via talismans/tiaras or the Abyss unlocked by Enter the Abyss. Bank space for the nine Lunar equipment pieces. Ask Brundt for a <strong>seal of passage</strong> and wear it on Lunar Isle or its inhabitants will send you away. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Lunar_Diplomacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki item list and dialogue/puzzle details</a>.</p>
        <p>The long quest builds its own equipment set: turn a dramen staff into a Lunar staff by taking it to the four elemental altars in order, mine/smith Lunar ore for the helm, kill <strong>level-111 Suqahs</strong> for a tooth and four hides, have the hides tanned and sew the garments, and recover the ring, amulet and other pieces through the island tasks. Rebank before Suqahs with antipoison, food and a suitable combat style. Wear <strong>all nine Lunar pieces</strong> to enter Dream World. There, complete the trials and final fight; regular armour, weapons, staves and potions are disallowed, but food and runes are permitted. If you leave, prepare new kindling to return. The Wiki is useful for the trial order rather than guessing dialogue.</p>
        <p>Finish for the <strong>Lunar spellbook</strong>, Lunar Isle/astral access, 50 astral runes and quest XP. Lunar is a second spellbook with travel/support spells; it does not erase the standard spellbook. Switch back to standard spells when you need High Alchemy or enchantments. Keep the seal/staff accessible for later island travel.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Check the lantern, herbs and a usable route into all four altars">
          <p>Extinguish the bullseye or sapphire lantern before fitting the quest's emerald lens, then relight it. If the body is missing, buy a replacement from Miltog in Dorgesh-Kaan and fuel it with Lumbridge swamp tar at the adjacent still. Keep the removed sapphire/lens. Dommik sells the needle and thread; the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> explains how to replace <strong>one guam and one marrentill</strong>. The Oneiromancer provides the special potion vial; four Suqah hides and the tooth come from the quest's Suqah kills.</p>
          <p><strong>For the four altar visits:</strong> take an air, fire, water and earth talisman/tiara already in the bank, and use the dramen staff at the altars in <strong>air → fire → water → earth</strong> order. For missing talismans, the matching elemental wizards south of Falador, northwest of Port Sarim, can drop them; kill only the needed type until its talisman is obtained, without assuming a fixed kill count.</p>
          <p>The already-unlocked <strong>Abyss</strong> is the alternative to collecting talismans. The Mage of Zamorak north of Edgeville is in the Wilderness, and entry drains Prayer and normally skulls you: bank valuables, take the staff plus a cheap pickaxe and teleport, and use the appropriate inner rift. Rebank and restore Prayer before later combat. If the dramen staff was lost, get a new branch from the Entrana dungeon tree and use a knife on it; bank prohibited equipment for the boat and obtain an axe from the dungeon zombies.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Quests before the RFD finale</div><h2>Finish useful quests before returning to the council.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i24-chompy" number="4" title="Complete Big Chompy Bird Hunting and keep its gear">
        <p>This is required for both the <strong>Lumbridge Guide</strong> and <strong>Skrach Uglogwee</strong> RFD chapters. Reach <strong>Rantz</strong> in the eastern Feldip Hills (fairy ring <strong>AKS</strong> nearby). Bring an axe, knife, chisel, <strong>100 feathers, four wolf bones</strong> and food; the quest teaches you to make ogre-arrow shafts from achey logs, tips from wolf bones and then ogre arrows, and gives you an <strong>ogre bow</strong>. Follow Rantz's family story and cook the quest bird on his spit. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Big_Chompy_Bird_Hunting" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki quest walkthrough</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>The unusual hunting loop:</strong> take <strong>ogre bellows</strong> from the chest in Rantz's cave, fill them from the nearby <strong>swamp bubbles</strong>, use them on local swamp toads to make <strong>bloated toads</strong>, then drop those as bait in the hunting area. A chompy may land; shoot it with the ogre bow and ogre arrows. Repeat for the quest's required bird, rather than grinding diary kill counts. Bank the <strong>bellows, ogre bow, arrows and at least one extra raw chompy</strong> for Skrach later.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Supply the arrows and collect only the ingredients Rantz requests">
          <p>Buy <strong>100 feathers</strong> from Gerrant's fishing shop in Port Sarim. Kill four wolves for their <strong>wolf bones</strong>; White Wolf Mountain has lower-level wolves if the level-64 Feldip ones are uncomfortable. Use your axe and knife on local achey trees/logs for shafts, attach the feathers, chisel the bones into arrow tips, and finish the arrows.</p>
          <p>The family chooses from quest-local <strong>onion, tomato, potato, cabbage, equa leaves and doogle leaves</strong>. Follow the requested ingredients: onion/tomato/cabbage/doogle are west of Rantz, while potato/equa are southeast. The bellows come from the cave chest. Catch and bank a separate raw chompy for Skrach after Rantz's cooked bird has been handed in.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-murder" number="5" title="Complete Murder Mystery">
        <p>Go to <strong>Sinclair Mansion</strong> north of Seers' Village and speak to the guard. Bring <strong>one empty pot</strong> (buy a replacement from Lumbridge's general store). There is no combat; the kitchen flour barrel supplies flour for your pot and the west shed's sacks supply flypaper: collect the dagger, thread, poison and suspect evidence in the mansion, use flour/flypaper for fingerprints, then present the matching case. Finish the investigation before moving to the next quest. It supplies <strong>three Quest Points</strong> and closes both the Lumbridge Guide and later King's Ransom prerequisites. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Murder_Mystery" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki evidence walkthrough</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-cold-war" number="6" title="Complete Cold War for the later Weiss quest">
        <p><strong>Why now:</strong> Cold War is a prerequisite for <em>Making Friends with My Arm</em>, which you will complete in 2.6. It also awards one Quest Point. Talk to <strong>Larry at Ardougne Zoo</strong>. Bring 10 oak planks, 10 steel nails, hammer, spade, a normal plank, silk, a steel bar/clockwork mechanism, raw cod or an activated ring of charos, swamp tar, five ordinary feathers, one mahogany plank and leather; obtain the cowbell during the quest. <strong>Build the required crafting table 3 before the clockwork-penguin step:</strong> in your POH workshop, upgrade the crafting table 2 built for birdhouses with <strong>2 molten glass</strong> at 34 Construction (already exceeded). Check how much glass remains after the fishbowl, lanterns and lighthouse; make only the shortfall from <strong>1 bucket of sand + 1 soda ash</strong> at a furnace. If the old table was removed, rebuild table 1 with <strong>4 oak planks</strong>, upgrade to table 2 with <strong>1 molten glass</strong>, then use 2 more glass for table 3. A study or kitchen does not substitute for the workshop. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Cold_War" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki quest details</a>.</p>
        <p>Larry takes you to the iceberg to build a bird hide; watch and record the penguins' greeting emotes. Make the clockwork penguin at your POH crafting table, wear the disguise to infiltrate the colony, gather the cowbell and make the penguin bongos, then clear the ice course and Icelord encounter. Bring some food and complete the course at your current Agility level. Finish the quest, but leave Making Friends itself for the later 70s block.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Replace missing penguin and building materials">
          <p>Count <strong>10 unnoted oak planks, 10 steel nails, one regular plank, one silk, one clockwork mechanism or steel bar, one swamp tar, five feathers, one mahogany plank and one leather</strong>. The <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/#i22-dragon-slayer`}> small-material suppliers</a> covers nails, glass, ordinary planks and steel; sawmill conversion costs 250 coins per oak plank and 1,500 per mahogany plank. Cut a mahogany log north of the Farming Guild if no log remains. Buy silk in Al Kharid, tan a cowhide with Ellis there for normal leather, and buy feathers from Gerrant.</p>
          <p>If no finished clockwork remains, use <strong>one steel bar on crafting table 2 or better</strong> to make it; then use the required table 3 for the penguin. This mechanism is separate from any clockworks still being used for birdhouses. Your <strong>activated ring of charos</strong> from Garden of Tranquillity can replace the raw-cod payment; without it, big-net fish at Catherby until you catch <strong>one raw cod</strong>. Keep the ring equipped for that dialogue, and collect the cowbell during the quest.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-trio" number="7" title="Complete Tai Bwo Wannai Trio and unlock karambwans">
        <p>This is not an RFD requirement, but the <strong>permanent karambwan food loop</strong> makes it worth doing before Cooking 70. Start with <strong>Timfraku</strong> in Tai Bwo Wannai, then help his three sons around Karamja. Pack an <strong>agility potion (4)</strong>—Tamayu requires the full four-dose item, not merely an available boost—an <strong>iron-or-better spear</strong>, small fishing net, hammer, at least 30 coins for quest payments, knife, pestle and mortar, tinderbox, two logs or an axe, jogre bones, seaweed, a banana and Karamjan rum, plus Magic/Ranged gear for a monkey, antipoison and travel supplies. Jogres can supply the bones and sometimes a spear; if needed, an iron-or-better spear can be bought at the Fortis Blacksmith. Combine the sliced banana with the rum <strong>before leaving Karamja</strong>. Follow the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Tai_Bwo_Wannai_Trio" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki's item/order details</a> for the odd recipe chain rather than guessing.</p>
        <p><strong>Make the Agility potions and save a spare:</strong> at 34+ Herblore, each <strong>toadflax + vial of water + toad's legs</strong> makes an Agility potion(3). If no toadflax is banked, take <strong>200 coins, food and light gear</strong> to the <strong>Brimhaven Agility Arena</strong> in east Brimhaven. Pay Cap'n Izzy No-Beard to enter, traverse ordinary obstacles to tag the currently lit ticket dispenser, and repeat until you have <strong>three Brimhaven vouchers per missing toadflax</strong>; Pirate Jackie the Fruit's <strong>Agility Arena Store</strong> exchanges them for the herb. Each successful tag gives one voucher; there is no seed roll or crop timer. If you prefer passive preparation, a Master Farmer can yield a variable toadflax seed to grow at the disease-free Hosidius herb patch, or use the arena if you want to gather the herb now. At the <strong>Tree Gnome Stronghold swamp</strong>, collect toads from the ground and remove their legs; the spirit-tree network already reaches the Stronghold. Make enough three-dose potions to decant into <strong>one full four-dose bottle for Trio</strong> and a separate <strong>four-dose reserve for Making Friends with My Arm</strong> in 2.6; from zero, <strong>three herbs and three sets of legs</strong> make nine doses, enough for two four-dose bottles with one dose spare. Use a potion decanter or combine doses at the bank. Do not spend the reserved bottle on ordinary travel.</p>
        <p><strong>The useful unlock during the quest:</strong> catch stackable <strong>karambwanji</strong> with the small net at the Holy Lake, take 20 to <strong>Lubufu</strong> south-east of Brimhaven, and receive a <strong>karambwan vessel</strong>. Load it with karambwanji; at 65+ Fishing, already reached, fish a raw karambwan on Karamja's north-east coast. For Tamayu, cook one into a <em>poison</em> karambwan and grind it to poison the spear—do not eat it. His hunt then succeeds. Tinsay's burnt-jogre-bone/karambwanji sauce and Tiadeche's vessel/manual errands complete the other two branches. Return to Timfraku, then talk to <strong>Tinsay</strong> in the village to claim the 5,000 Cooking XP and the ability to cook edible karambwans. Keep a vessel for later fishing.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Keep the unusual food ingredients separate from ordinary combat food">
          <p>Buy an <strong>iron-or-better spear</strong> from the Fortis Blacksmith if you do not own a suitable spear; you can also use a suitable spear dropped by a jogre. Kill a jogre for its bones and a monkey with Magic or Ranged for the skin/corpse step. Collect seaweed from Karamja's shore, buy rum at Musa Point and pick a banana on its plantation; slice the banana with the knife and add it to the rum while still on Karamja.</p>
          <p>Catch <strong>more than the 20 karambwanji handed to Lubufu</strong>: the vessel needs bait and Tinsay's sauce needs more fish. After obtaining the vessel, keep fishing until the quest's raw karambwan and recipe ingredients are present. Follow the quest dialogue for burning the jogre bones and making the sauce. The Agility potion above must reach <strong>four doses after decanting</strong>; a three-dose bottle cannot pay Tamayu.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-one-small" number="8" title="Complete One Small Favour; put both lamps into Herblore">
        <p><strong>Why now:</strong> Swan Song needs it, and King's Ransom will need it later. Begin with <strong>Yanni Salika in Shilo Village</strong>, follow his red-mahogany request into the chain of favors, then reverse the chain to deliver the reward. <strong>Prepare:</strong> four steel bars, one bronze and one iron bar; two guams, one marrentill and one harralander for Guthix rest; <strong>an empty cup and bowl of hot water</strong>; five pigeon cages (available by Jerico's house in East Ardougne); a pot and soft clay for its lid; hammer, chisel, pickaxe, food and teleports. The gem repair uses opal, jade, red topaz and sapphire—bring two cut of each if banked or use a chisel on the quest's uncut gems and replace any crushed ones. Withdraw per region rather than carrying everything all at once. The <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/One_Small_Favour" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current quest guide</a> has the dialogue/delivery order and bank breaks. Bank between regions and work through the chain at your own pace. Make an <strong>extra pot lid</strong> while the recipe is unlocked if you want to reuse it for Swan Song.</p>
        <p>The two selectable lamps give <strong>10,000 XP each</strong> in a skill at level 30 or above. Your <strong>40+ Herblore</strong> qualifies, so use <strong>both on Herblore</strong>. Their combined 20,000 XP helps toward the later 50 and 70 requirements; check your new level afterward.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Make the requested Guthix rest and recover crushed gems">
          <p>Get the <strong>empty cup</strong> by drinking the tea in the house north of Sanfew in Taverley. Take a bowl from Lumbridge castle, fill it with water, then heat it on a range. Use the <strong>bowl of hot water on the empty cup</strong>, then add <strong>two guams, one marrentill and one harralander</strong> to make Guthix rest(3). Ordinary restore or prayer potions cannot replace this tea. Refill missing herbs through the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a>.</p>
          <p>Use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/#i22-dragon-slayer`}> small-material suppliers</a> for <strong>four steel bars, one bronze bar, one iron bar, an empty pot and fresh soft clay</strong>. Take all five pigeon cages from behind Jerico's house in East Ardougne. When the quest teaches pot lids, shape one from soft clay at a pottery wheel and fire it in the pottery oven; make a second only if you are reserving it for Swan Song.</p>
          <p>The gnome lamps provide uncut <strong>opal, jade, red topaz and sapphire</strong>. Cut and replace those; if a gem is crushed, buy another from <strong>Gnormadium Avlafrim</strong> at the landing strip or mine replacements at Shilo. Bring a few thousand coins for the repair fallback in case a gem needs replacing.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-cooking-62" number="9" title="Reach 62 Cooking for Swan Song">
        <p>Swan Song asks for 62 Cooking. After claiming Tai Bwo Wannai Trio's 5,000 Cooking XP, check whether you still need training from Chapter 1's 60 Cooking. Cook banked raw fish or begin the karambwan loop below until the skill tab reads <strong>62</strong>. Use a range to reduce burns; the Lumbridge Castle range and cellar chest are already accessible through RFD's introduction. Pause at 62 for Swan Song, then return to Cooking for Awowogei's 70 requirement.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-swan" number="10" title="Complete Swan Song and open Piscatoris">
        <p>Check <strong>One Small Favour</strong> above and Chapter 1's <strong>Garden of Tranquillity</strong>, 100+ QP, 62 Cooking, 62 Fishing, 45 Smithing, 42 Firemaking and 40 Crafting. Those non-Magic skills are already covered. Swan Song's <strong>66 Magic is boostable</strong>: the battlestaff alchs brought you to at least 65, so take a <strong>Wizard's mind bomb (+3 Magic)</strong> for the requirement check rather than grinding a whole Magic level. If your unboosted Magic has reached 66 from other play, no boost is needed. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Swan_Song" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki quest details</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Bring:</strong> 10 mist runes, 10 lava runes, five blood runes, a lidded pot (or two soft clay to make pot and lid), five iron bars, logs, tinderbox, hammer, food, prayer restore, combat gear and a small fishing net. <strong>If the combination runes are missing, return to the already-unlocked Mage Training Arena north of Emir's Arena.</strong> The upstairs rewards shop sells each mist or lava rune for <strong>1 Telekinetic, 1 Graveyard, 15 Enchantment and 1 Alchemist pizazz point</strong>; for a zero-stock 10+10 purchase, earn <strong>20/20/300/20 points</strong> respectively, then buy the exact shortfall. This lets you buy the missing runes directly; ordinary Wizards' Guild rune shops do not stock combination runes. Buy the five blood runes from a stocked rune shop if needed. Seven bones can be obtained during the quest. Reach the <strong>Piscatoris Fishing Colony</strong> by Kathy Corkat's boat west of Tree Gnome Stronghold (50 coins or ring of charos) or fairy ring <strong>AKQ</strong> and a walk. Help the Wise Old Man defend and repair the colony, bank before the level-170 <strong>Sea Troll Queen</strong>, and use an appropriate ranged or Magic setup with food; she uses multiple styles and drains Prayer. Finish for Piscatoris access and its monkfish fishery, another useful food option. Cook your catches when you want more food and Cooking XP.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Check the lidded pot, bars and runes before leaving">
          <p>The pot and lid are separate from One Small Favour's hand-in. If no spare lidded pot remains, shape and fire <strong>one pot and one pot lid from two soft clay</strong> at Rimmington's pottery facilities; One Small Favour just unlocked the lid recipe. Smelt iron ore until <strong>five iron bars</strong> are ready, using the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/#i22-dragon-slayer`}> small-material suppliers</a>. Buy a small fishing net from Gerrant and cut one ordinary log.</p>
          <p>Buy the <strong>five blood runes</strong> from a rune shop that stocks them, such as the Wizards' Guild once your current Magic reaches 66 (a Falador mind bomb can supply the access boost). Buy any missing mist/lava runes at MTA as described above. If more MTA points are needed, refill law and nature runes at the Wizards' Guild, cosmic runes at Baba Yaga on the now-unlocked Lunar Isle, and the rooms' elemental runes at either shop; use the MTA room instructions from Chapter 1.4 and restore prayer/antipoison via the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> before the queen.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <ExpandableNote label="Optional early unlock" title="Making Friends with My Arm can wait until 2.6">
        <p>If you independently have or can comfortably boost <strong>68 Agility and 72 Mining</strong>, have <strong>66 Firemaking and 35 Construction</strong>, and completed Swan Song, Cold War and My Arm's Big Adventure, you may do Making Friends now for the disease-free Weiss herb patch and large XP rewards. It is <strong>not required in 2.4</strong>; 2.6 includes it alongside the training for Song of the Elves' 70 Agility and Mining requirements. You can finish this chapter without doing it early. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Making_Friends_with_My_Arm" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki requirements</a>.</p>
      </ExpandableNote>

      <RouteStep id="i24-cooking-70" number="11" title="Build a useful food stock and reach 70 Cooking">
        <p><strong>Why 70:</strong> King Awowogei's RFD chapter requires it. The game allows a boost, but train to <strong>unboosted 70</strong> here so the requirement and a durable food stock are both solved. Check banked raw fish from Tempoross and other play first. Cook those before catching more; gutting leaping fish during Barbarian Fishing gives a little Cooking XP but does not leave the same raw-fish stock.</p>
        <p><strong>Recommended relaxed loop:</strong> take the retained <strong>karambwan vessel</strong> and stackable <strong>karambwanji bait</strong>. Net more karambwanji at the Holy Lake near Tai Bwo Wannai, bait the vessel, fish raw karambwan at the north-east Karamja shore (fairy ring <strong>DKP</strong> nearby), bank a comfortable batch, then cook normally on a range. Select <strong>cooked/edible karambwan</strong>, not the poison preparation used during the quest. The Hosidius Kitchen offers a nearby bank and reduced burns <em>if</em> you independently completed the Easy Kourend & Kebos diary; check that the diary is complete before using its burn reduction. The <strong>Lumbridge Castle range</strong> is an available option with reduced burns, with the RFD chest in the cellar. Expect burns and fish enough to cover them. Use the ordinary automatic cooking action. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ironman_Guide/Cooking" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki Ironman Cooking</a>.</p>
        <p>Already-banked fish or ordinary leaping-fish gutting can fill the gap if you prefer; You already have at least 65 Fishing, so choose whichever method you enjoy or which supplies the food you need. Check your Cooking level after each batch and stop at <strong>unboosted 70</strong>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i24-cooking-methods" informational={true} skill="Cooking" target="70, unboosted" why="Awowogei needs 70 Cooking; training with fish also stocks your bank for the coming fights." recommended="Normal fish-and-cook karambwan batches after Tai Bwo Wannai Trio, creating a useful PvM food bank." resource="Cook existing Tempoross and other raw fish first at the Lumbridge Castle range; use the Hosidius Kitchen only if its diary is already done." relaxed="Ordinary Barbarian Fishing with automatic inventory gutting offers a change of pace and a little Cooking XP." />
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Finish the council</div><h2>Five members remain; the first three were freed in Chapter 1.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i24-legends-access" number="12" title="Verify 107 QP and start Legends' Quest for Kharazi access">
        <p><strong>Check for 107 Quest Points:</strong> completing the earlier chapters gives you <strong>181 QP before 2.4</strong> and <strong>196 QP after Swan Song</strong>, so you should already qualify. Family Crest, Heroes' Quest, Shilo Village, Underground Pass and the rest of the Legends prerequisite chain are already complete. Bring an axe, machete, <strong>charcoal and at least three papyrus</strong> (bring spares because they can break), jungle supplies/antipoison and travel items to <strong>Radimus Erkle at the Legends' Guild</strong>. Take his notes, enter the Kharazi Jungle south of Shilo Village and use the notes to map the three areas. The route's 70 Woodcutting covers the jungle step. Keep the <strong>Radimus notes</strong> for later entry and collect a <strong>vanilla pod</strong> in the south-west jungle for Sir Amik. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Legends%27_Quest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki partial-start map instructions</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Stop after access and the vanilla pod.</strong> You can free Sir Amik after this partial start. Leave full Legends' Quest and its 45-Herblore requirement until 2.5. A started quest gives <strong>zero Quest Points</strong> until completed.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Buy the jungle mapping kit at its accessible supplier">
          <p>If the bank lacks a machete, charcoal or papyrus, buy them from <strong>Jiminua's Jungle Store northwest of Tai Bwo Wannai</strong>. Bring <strong>at least three papyrus</strong> and spare charcoal/papyrus for failed mapping attempts, plus an axe. Radimus supplies his notes at the Legends' Guild; keep them after mapping. Collect the vanilla pod in the Kharazi Jungle now, and bank it for Sir Amik.</p>
          <p>Keep the gems, gold bars and unpowered orbs for the full Legends' Quest trip in 2.5; you only need the mapping supplies here.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-guide" number="13" title="Free the Lumbridge Guide">
        <p>Big Chompy and Murder Mystery are now complete; Biohazard, Demon Slayer, Nature Spirit and Witch's House were finished in Chapter 1. Take a <strong>bucket of milk, egg, pot of flour and cake tin</strong> (milk, egg and flour are sold at the Culinaromancer's Chest; buy a missing cake tin from a charter-ship trader), inspect the frozen Guide in Lumbridge Castle and visit <strong>Wizard Traiborn</strong> at the Wizards' Tower. He enchants the three ingredients through quest-memory questions and item puzzles; use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Recipe_for_Disaster/Freeing_the_Lumbridge_Guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki quiz guide</a> when the randomized question needs a reminder. Make/bake the cake of guidance, return it to the Guide and confirm the subquest's one QP.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Use one fresh set of the three cake ingredients">
          <p>Count <strong>one bucket of milk, one egg, one pot of flour and a cake tin</strong> after earlier RFD cooking. The chest supplies the three food ingredients, and charter crews sell cake tins. Traiborn enchants this set during the quiz. Keep the tin for future baking; buy another set of ingredients for Sir Amik's mixture later.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-evil-dave" number="14" title="Free Evil Dave with a measured spice stew">
        <p>Gertrude's Cat and Shadow of the Storm are already complete. <strong>Do not trade away the grown cat reserved by the optional cat loop in 1.1 for death runes before this subquest.</strong> Bring a <strong>grown cat or hellcat</strong> (not an overgrown cat; a kitten catches slowly) and up to <strong>nine ordinary stews</strong>. If your only cat is still a kitten, let it mature while doing the preceding quests or accept a much slower catch rate; allow extra time if you need to raise a new kitten. Inspect Dave at the table, then go to <strong>Doris's house west of Edgeville bank</strong> and descend into the basement. Tell Dave the magic requires him to describe the stew. Your cat catches <strong>hell-rats</strong>, which drop brown, red, yellow or orange spice shakers. This is a cat-and-recipe puzzle, not combat training. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Recipe_for_Disaster/Freeing_Evil_Dave" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki spice procedure</a>.</p>
        <p>For each colour, test a stew containing <strong>one dose of that colour only</strong>. Dave says whether a spice amount is correct. If not, test two; if neither one nor two works, the needed amount is three. Write down all four results, then combine the exact doses on a final stew. Finish Dave's dialogue and <strong>use</strong> the stew on frozen Dave in Lumbridge; do not eat it. Keep surplus spice only if you want later stew boosts—the route does not depend on them.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Replace missing stews and give a replacement kitten time to grow">
          <p>Buy stews at the <strong>Forester's Arms in Seers' Village</strong>, or make them: put a potato and cooked meat into a bowl of water, then cook the uncooked stew on a range (25 Cooking). Buy a bowl or make one from soft clay, pick potatoes from the field north of Lumbridge, and cook beef from a cow. Refill failed/tested stews until your final recipe is ready.</p>
          <p>If the reserved cat was traded away, buy a replacement kitten from <strong>Gertrude for 100 coins</strong>. Feed and interact with it while doing other quests until it grows; there is no bank item or potion that skips its growth. Keep the grown cat for Icthlarin and A Tail of Two Cats in 2.6.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-skrach" number="15" title="Free Skrach Uglogwee with a cooked jubbly">
        <p>Retrieve the banked <strong>ogre bellows, ogre bow/arrows, extra raw chompy</strong> and an <strong>iron spit</strong>. Bring an axe, any log, tinderbox, pickaxe and a ball of wool; the quest's 41 Cooking and 20 Firemaking are covered. Inspect Skrach, talk to <strong>Rantz</strong> by Feldip Hills, cut his boat-tree twice, then go to the marked Karamja landing (fairy ring <strong>CKR</strong> is nearby). Cook the raw chompy on the spit/fire by the arrow-marked tree to call the boat, cross, and report back to Rantz. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Recipe_for_Disaster/Freeing_Skrach_Uglogwee" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki boat/jubbly sequence</a>.</p>
        <p>For the jubbly, take a <strong>bloated toad</strong> from Rantz's swamp, a nearby rock and the ball of wool. Use charged bellows on the bloated toad to make a <strong>balloon toad</strong>, drop it as bait and shoot the spawned jubbly with ogre arrows. Spawn/kill again if needed; cook the raw jubbly on Rantz's spit-roast, then use the cooked bird on Skrach in Lumbridge. Keep the chompy equipment banked afterward in case you want to hunt again.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Rebuild the spit and hunting consumables if the saved kit is incomplete">
          <p>Smith <strong>one iron bar into an iron spit</strong> at an anvil with a hammer (17 Smithing). The <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/#i22-dragon-slayer`}> small-material suppliers</a> covers ore, wool, tools and replacement ropes elsewhere. Shear and spin extra wool if repeated balloon-toad baits consume your last ball.</p>
          <p>Take replacement bellows from <strong>Rantz's cave chest</strong> and buy another ogre bow from Rantz if yours was lost. Remake arrows with achey logs, feathers and wolf bones using the earlier Chompy step. If the extra raw chompy was cooked or discarded, repeat that same bloated-toad hunting loop until <strong>one raw chompy</strong> is banked. Hunt another jubbly if the cooked quest bird burns.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-sir-amik" number="16" title="Free Sir Amik Varze; leave Legends only partly done">
        <p>Check your <strong>107+ Quest Points</strong>, started Legends' Quest, Kharazi access and vanilla pod. Inspect Sir Amik and <strong>ask the Lumbridge Cook about him</strong> before visiting the Wise Old Man. Gather a bucket of milk, pot of cream, pot of cornflour (mill raw sweetcorn if needed), vanilla pod, <strong>dramen branch</strong>, pestle and mortar, <strong>ice gloves</strong>, dramen/Lunar staff and an ordinary <strong>raw chicken</strong>. Assemble the crème brûlée ingredients in the Cook's order. If Swan Song dialogue temporarily masks the Wise Old Man's Evil Chicken option, finish Swan Song first—which this route already did. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Recipe_for_Disaster/Freeing_Sir_Amik_Varze" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki ingredient and fight details</a>.</p>
        <p>Ask the Wise Old Man about strange beasts/the Evil Chicken. Bank in <strong>Zanaris</strong>, then enter the Evil Chicken's Lair by using raw chicken on its shrine. Bring an <strong>anti-dragon shield</strong>, food, prayer restore, antipoison as needed and Magic/Ranged supplies. Kill a <strong>level-227 black dragon</strong> for its token—safespots exist—then the Evil Chicken for its egg. Use the safespots and restock if the fight is taking longer than expected. Finish the brûlée with egg and crushed dramen-branch cinnamon; use the token/dragonfire step as the quest directs, with ice gloves, and deliver it to Sir Amik. Full Legends completion remains deferred.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Gather raw sweetcorn and an uncarved dramen branch">
          <p>Buy <strong>one bucket of milk, one pot of cream and one raw chicken</strong> from the Culinaromancer's Chest. For the cornflour, pick <strong>one raw sweetcorn from the fields in Outer Fortis</strong>, south of Civitas illa Fortis, and take it with an empty pot to a working windmill. Put the corn in the hopper, operate the hopper controls and collect the cornflour below. A bowl of cooked sweetcorn is a different item.</p>
          <p>If no uncarved <strong>dramen branch</strong> remains, return to Entrana's dungeon tree. Bank prohibited equipment before taking the boat; kill dungeon zombies for an axe and cut a fresh branch. The completed Lost City fight need not be repeated. Keep your dramen/Lunar staff for Zanaris and crush the <em>branch</em> with a pestle and mortar for the cinnamon.</p>
          <p>The vanilla pod was collected during the Legends access step; recover another from the southwest Kharazi Jungle with axe, machete and Radimus notes if needed. Replace lost ice gloves through the Ice Queen route in Heroes' Quest and a missing anti-dragon shield through Duke Horacio. Refill the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> before entering the lair.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-awowogei" number="17" title="Free King Awowogei at 70 Cooking">
        <p>Check <strong>unboosted 70 Cooking</strong>, 48+ Agility and Chapter 2.2's Monkey Madness I. Inspect Awowogei, take the retained <strong>M'speak amulet and Karamjan monkey greegree</strong> to Ape Atoll, and talk to the <strong>three wise monkeys</strong> in the temple. They explain that a big snake must be stuffed with a <strong>red banana</strong> and <strong>tchiki monkey nuts</strong>, not ordinary banana/nuts. Bring <strong>one ordinary banana and one monkey nuts</strong> for the first monkey conversations, at least <strong>3,000 coins</strong> for three blank talismans if needed, rope, knife, pestle and mortar, food, antipoison and combat gear. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Recipe_for_Disaster/Freeing_King_Awowogei" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki full subquest</a>.</p>
        <p>Make <strong>gorilla, ninja and zombie greegrees</strong> if not already owned: get three blank talismans, the corresponding monkey bones and take them to Zooknock in the Ape Atoll dungeon. Gorilla form reaches the red-banana tree, ninja form traverses the agility course for tchiki nuts, and zombie form crosses the temple's hot coals. On <strong>Crash Island</strong>, kill level-84 big snakes in the pit for corpses; turn on Protect from Melee before entering. Take several corpses and ingredients because the stuffed snake can burn even at 70. Slice banana, grind nuts, stuff the corpses, then cook on the <strong>long hot rock</strong> past the temple coals. Use the successfully cooked snake on Awowogei in Lumbridge while wearing M'speak. Do not eat it.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Supply the three talismans and the ordinary food test before the special meal">
          <p>Buy the <strong>ordinary banana and monkey nuts from Solihib in Ape Atoll's market</strong>, and use them on the wise monkeys when asked. They lead to the red-banana/tchiki-nut correction; arriving only with the final special ingredients skips a required earlier interaction. <strong>Tutab's Magical Market</strong> sells blank monkey talismans for <strong>1,000 coins each</strong>; buy one for each missing gorilla, ninja and zombie greegree.</p>
          <p>Use the matching <strong>gorilla, ninja-monkey and zombie-monkey bones</strong> with those talismans at Zooknock: gorillas are temple guards, ninja monkeys guard the village, and zombie monkeys are in the temple basement. Rebank prayer and antipoison for the dungeon with the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a>. If the <strong>M'speak amulet</strong> is lost, use the full <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/#i22-monkey-madness`}>MM1 amulet-replacement instructions</a>. A missing Karamjan greegree needs a fresh monkey talisman and ordinary Karamja monkey bones at Zooknock. Use another retained greegree to trade with Tutab; if all disguises are missing, repeat the <strong>monkey child's lost-toy/talisman conversation</strong> from MM1 with M'speak equipped, using five garden bananas if requested. A missing <strong>ninja greegree</strong> later needs one new talisman plus bones from a ninja monkey guarding Marim, taken to the same Zooknock; the completed subquest does not remove that recovery route.</p>
          <p>Get a few <strong>snake corpses, red bananas and tchiki nuts</strong> for cooking retries; stop once one cooked stuffed snake is ready. Keep all three new greegrees afterward for later Ape Atoll quests.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-final-gate" number="18" title="Check all council members and 175+ Quest Points before the finale">
        <p>Before entering the final portal, open the quest list. The four Chapter 1.3 credits (RFD introduction + Goblin, Dwarf and Pirate), the five members on this page, and the standalone prerequisites must all be complete. Completing the quests above gives you <strong>201 QP before the finale</strong>, well above its <strong>175-QP</strong> requirement. You can reach that total with Making Friends and full Legends still unfinished. If your total is lower, check the earlier quest steps for anything you skipped or have yet to finish.</p>
        <p>Also verify <strong>Desert Treasure I and Horror from the Deep</strong>, both already finished, and prepare a bank of food, restores, <strong>ice gloves</strong>, Magic/Ranged gear and suitable runes. Choose combat gear for your current Magic, Ranged and Hitpoints levels. You can switch styles and restock between bosses.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-culinaromancer" number="19" title="Defeat the Culinaromancer and buy Barrows gloves">
        <p>Enter the Lumbridge Castle dining-room portal after the <strong>175-QP check</strong>. The fights are instanced; <strong>Prayer is disabled</strong>, but you can leave and bank/restock <strong>between individual bosses</strong>. Bring substantial food and play each encounter separately. Agrith-Na-Na, Flambeed, Karamel, Dessourt and the Gelatinnoth Mother do not all favour one style: bring Magic/Ranged options, including an upgraded Iban's staff if you meet its Attack and Magic requirements. Wear <strong>ice gloves for Flambeed</strong>; Karamel drains stats, so restores help; the Mother changes vulnerabilities and rewards the elemental/style switches learned in Horror from the Deep. The final Culinaromancer hits hard but has low Defence. Use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Recipe_for_Disaster/Defeating_the_Culinaromancer" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki boss notes</a> for detailed attack cues. You can prepare and attempt each fight with the levels you have reached so far.</p>
        <p>Completion adds <strong>one Quest Point</strong> for <strong>202 QP after this chapter's quests</strong> and full chest access. Buy <strong>Barrows gloves for 130,000 coins</strong> from the Culinaromancer's Chest in the Lumbridge cellar. They are a strong all-style glove upgrade; put them in your normal combat kit. The final <strong>20,000-XP antique lamp</strong> requires a skill <strong>at level 50 or above</strong> and <strong>can be banked</strong>. Prefer Herblore when eligible; if it is still below the lamp threshold, <strong>bank and reserve the lamp for Herblore after reaching 50</strong>. Do not click a different skill just to clear the inventory.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Restock for one boss at a time, with ordinary restores for Karamel">
          <p>At the bank before Karamel, count <strong>ordinary restore-potion doses</strong>, food and runes for a spell you can still cast after a stat drain. At 22 Herblore, each clean harralander + vial of water + red spiders' eggs makes restore(3); the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> supplies missing ingredients. Prayer potions do not repair those stats, and Prayer is disabled in these fights.</p>
          <p>Recover missing ice gloves from the Ice Queen before Flambeed. Rebuild the food bank with the karambwan fishing/cooking loop above if earlier attempts used it; return to the chest between bosses instead of budgeting one inventory for the entire sequence. Keep <strong>130,000 coins</strong> separate for the gloves purchase after completion.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">2.4 exit check</div>
        <h3>Lunar spells, a stocked food bank and Barrows gloves are ready.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>The Fremennik Isles</strong> complete and Helm of Neitiznot kept; <strong>unboosted 60 Mining</strong>, Lunar Diplomacy and the Lunar spellbook unlocked.</li>
          <li>Big Chompy, Murder Mystery, Cold War, Tai Bwo Wannai Trio, One Small Favour and Swan Song complete; <strong>both One Small Favour lamps used on Herblore</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>Unboosted 70 Cooking</strong> verified, with banked fish/karambwans according to your chosen method; Piscatoris and the karambwan loop open.</li>
          <li><strong>Legends' Quest started and Kharazi Jungle accessible</strong>, but full Legends need not be complete. All five remaining RFD council members and the Culinaromancer finished; <strong>202 Quest Points from the guide and Barrows gloves owned</strong>.</li>
          <li>Use the RFD 20,000-XP lamp on Herblore only if eligible; otherwise bank it for Herblore after reaching 50. <strong>Making Friends with My Arm is deferred to 2.6</strong> unless you voluntarily did it early.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Next, take the new gloves and food into the combat and Morytania quests in 2.5. That chapter also includes the training you need for Piety and full Legends' Quest.</p>
      </section>

